1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,440
I'd been driving for
almost 11 hours when the

2
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:16,220
detour signs pushed me off the interstate.

3
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:21,720
The road narrowed to two lanes, the radio
lost its station, and for a long time the

4
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:23,880
only light out there
was my own headlights.

5
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:28,540
Around two in the morning I saw a gas
station sign glowing over the fields.

6
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:34,140
The pumps were on, the store was dark, and
there was one other car parked by the air

7
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:37,020
machine with its engine
running and nobody inside.

8
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:40,100
This was six years ago, in October.

9
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:43,840
I was 24 and moving back
home to Missouri after

10
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:46,160
a job in Colorado fell
apart, with everything

11
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,460
I owned in the backseat of a
Corolla with a cracked windshield.

12
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,240
I kept telling myself
one more hour, and by the

13
00:00:52,240 --> 00:00:54,120
time the detour came up, I was too tired

14
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:55,260
to be smart about it.

15
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:58,220
For a while there was
a pickup truck ahead of

16
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:00,360
me, the only other headlights for miles.

17
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:04,060
At a crossroads with no
signs at all, it turned

18
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,400
onto a dirt road, and its lights went out

19
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,200
almost at once.

20
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:10,740
It didn't park, it didn't
slow down that I could

21
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:13,180
see, the lights just went out, and the

22
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:15,000
dark closed over the
spot where it had been.

23
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:19,160
I kept going straight, because
the orange arrows told me to.

24
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:22,080
I pulled up to the pump
farthest from the other car.

25
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:26,360
It was an old station wagon, dark
green with wood panels on the sides.

26
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:28,980
Exhaust was rising from it in the cold.

27
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,820
The headlights were off,
but the dome light was

28
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:34,360
on, and I could see a
jacket on the passenger

29
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:36,440
seat and a fast food bag on the dashboard.

30
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,900
In the back, there was
a child's booster seat,

31
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:42,460
and a stuffed rabbit sitting in it, turned

32
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:43,780
around so it faced the rear window.

33
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:47,280
Two small sneakers sat on
the floor mat underneath,

34
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,740
side by side, like someone had taken them

35
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,400
off and meant to put them right back on.

36
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,360
I filled the tank and waited.

37
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:58,100
I think I wanted to see someone walk back
to that car, just so I could stop thinking

38
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:58,900
about it.

39
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:00,040
Nobody came.

40
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:03,280
The engine kept idling, steady,
like it had been running for hours.

41
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:06,760
Then, while I was watching,
the dome light went off.

42
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:10,700
I stood there with the nozzle in my
hand and stared at the dark windows.

43
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:13,260
A few seconds later, it came back on.

44
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:14,980
Nobody had opened a door.

45
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:18,900
I hung up the nozzle, got
back in my car, and left.

46
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:22,520
At the edge of the lot, I looked in
the rearview mirror one last time.

47
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:24,360
The dome light was still on.

48
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:27,740
The stuffed rabbit was facing forward now.

49
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,920
About twenty minutes later, the
detour signs ended at a truck stop.

50
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,280
The first real building I'd seen in hours.

51
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,420
The diner, a couple of
semis parked out back with

52
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:39,400
their running lights on, and a sign that

53
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:42,420
said Open 24 hours, with two
of the letters burned out.

54
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:47,200
I parked by the entrance because I needed
coffee, and I needed to be around people.

55
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:51,580
Inside it was warm and smelled like
burnt coffee and bacon grease.

56
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,580
There was a trucker at
the counter, reading

57
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:56,000
his phone, an old man asleep in a booth by

58
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,320
the window, and one waitress.

59
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,000
Her name tag said D.

60
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:01,460
She called me honey
before I'd even sat down.

61
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:05,300
I took a booth facing the door and
ordered coffee and a slice of pie.

62
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,380
That's when the couple came in.

63
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,500
They were young.

64
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:11,020
Maybe my age.

65
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:13,960
He wore a gray hoodie,
and she had on a denim

66
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,560
jacket that was too thin for the weather.

67
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,940
It had started to rain, and the shoulders
of both jackets were dark with it.

68
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:24,220
They were arguing in that low,
tight way people argue in public.

69
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:30,100
As they passed my booth, the girl said,
every single time, Ray, every single time.

70
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:31,820
He didn't answer.

71
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:34,940
They sat two booths down
from me, across the aisle,

72
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:37,480
and D. brought them menus and two waters.

73
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:41,320
I ate my pie and heard pieces
of their conversation,

74
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:44,300
something about a wrong
turn and whose idea

75
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,420
it was to leave so late.

76
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:49,660
At one point, Ray said, we'll
be fine, we're almost there.

77
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,660
She didn't say anything back.

78
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:55,120
When D. refilled my coffee,
she asked where I was headed.

79
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:56,340
I said Missouri.

80
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:58,500
She glanced out the window
and lowered her voice.

81
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,820
When you leave, honey, follow
the signs back to the interstate.

82
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:04,900
Don't take the old county road, even
if your phone says it's shorter.

83
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,520
I asked her why.

84
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:10,160
She smiled, said that road wasn't
kept up anymore, and walked away.

85
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:13,400
I got up to use the
restroom, at the end of a

86
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,280
short hallway past the kitchen, where one

87
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,320
of the lights kept flickering.

88
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:19,840
I was washing my hands when
I heard her voice through

89
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:22,320
the wall, from outside, from the parking

90
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:24,660
lot, every single time, Ray.

91
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:28,760
It was the same tired, angry
tone and the same words.

92
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:31,220
I turned off the water and listened.

93
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:34,260
A man's voice answered
her, too low to make out,

94
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:37,160
and then a car door shut, then nothing.

95
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,040
I stood there with my
wet hands out in front of

96
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:42,160
me, telling myself there was a window open

97
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:44,000
somewhere that sound carries.

98
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:49,260
When I came out and walked back toward my
booth, the bell over the front door rang.

99
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,340
It was them.

100
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:55,300
Gray hoodie, thin denim jacket,
both of them dark with rain.

101
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:57,740
They walked in the same
way, him a step ahead,

102
00:04:58,060 --> 00:05:00,280
her behind with her arms
crossed, and as they

103
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:04,060
passed me, she said, every single
time, Ray, every single time.

104
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:07,800
I stopped in the aisle and looked at
the booth where they'd been sitting.

105
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:08,960
It was empty.

106
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:12,500
No menus, no glasses, no
wet rings on the table.

107
00:05:12,940 --> 00:05:15,720
It had been wiped down like
nobody had used it all night.

108
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,160
They sat in that same booth.

109
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:21,020
Dee came over with two
menus and two waters,

110
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:23,680
smiled at them, and said, evening you two.

111
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,000
Rough night out there?

112
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,980
The way you'd greet
someone who just walked in.

113
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:30,720
I made myself walk past their
table on the way back to mine.

114
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:33,560
Up close, I could see
the rain on her jacket,

115
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,040
soaked into the denim in exactly the same

116
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:36,840
shape as before.

117
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:40,260
Ray had his wrist on the table,
and his watch caught the light.

118
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:42,580
It was an old digital watch.

119
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:47,120
It read 214, and the whole time
I stood there, it didn't change.

120
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:51,140
I sat down, and I watched
them have the same

121
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:54,120
conversation, wrong
turn, leaving too late.

122
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:57,120
The trucker never looked
up from his phone, and

123
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,060
the old man by the window never woke up.

124
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:02,100
Nobody else in that room seemed
to think anything was wrong.

125
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,040
I still don't know where
the nerve came from,

126
00:06:05,260 --> 00:06:07,020
but I walked over and stood at the end of

127
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:07,820
their table.

128
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:10,940
I asked, as normally as I could,
if they'd just gotten there.

129
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:13,620
The girl kept staring
out at the parking lot.

130
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:15,140
Ray looked up at me.

131
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:18,160
His eyes were red, like he hadn't
slept in a very long time.

132
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:21,580
Then he said, very calmly, we'll be fine.

133
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:22,840
We're almost there.

134
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:26,340
He said it to me, exactly
the way he'd said it to her.

135
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,460
Then Dee was beside me
with the coffee pot.

136
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:33,000
She put her hand on my arm,
very gently, and walked

137
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,700
me back to my booth like I was a little

138
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:36,200
kid who'd wandered off in a store.

139
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:38,880
Don't bother them,
honey, she said quietly.

140
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,400
They never stay long.

141
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:42,080
She filled my cup to the top.

142
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:44,740
I hadn't touched it since
the last time she filled it.

143
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,780
I left a twenty on the
table and walked out.

144
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:51,560
Outside the rain had stopped,
and the parking lot was dry.

145
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:53,180
Completely dry.

146
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,680
No puddles, no drops on my windshield.

147
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:58,760
I locked myself in my car
and sat there with the

148
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,660
engine running until the sky turned gray,

149
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,180
and then I followed the
signs back to the interstate,

150
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,040
exactly the way Dee told me to.

151
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:08,200
I didn't pass the gas
station on the way back.

152
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,400
I took the same road, I'm sure of that.

153
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,800
It just wasn't there anymore.

154
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:18,380
I had a cheap dash cam back then, the kind
that records over itself every few hours.

155
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:21,720
When I got home and checked it,
most of that night was gone.

156
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:27,060
The only file left starts as I pull into
the truck stop at 2.14 in the morning.

157
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:30,900
I park, the camera keeps
recording, and about

158
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:33,300
a minute later, the dark
green station wagon

159
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:35,600
pulls into the spot right in front of me.

160
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:39,580
Engine running, dome
light on, nobody inside.

161
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:43,340
The date on that clip is October 14th.

162
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:46,200
The year is the one before
I ever drove that road.

163
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,740
I still drive that interstate
a couple of times a year.

164
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:52,280
When the detour signs are
up, I don't take them.

165
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:55,480
I stop in the last town before
the exit, park somewhere

166
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:57,480
well lit, and sleep in my car until

167
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,280
morning.

